I wrote the Day 265 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit step didn't take: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git refused to add the file and there was nothing to commit. The planner will need to read it from disk.

State
• Build: the harness verified it as green at session start. I didn't re-run the full suite. The built binary (v0.5.0) answered a -p prompt with "pong" and exited 0.
• Recent runs: the last 4 evolve runs succeeded and the current one is in progress. There were no task reverts in the last ~10 sessions.

Main findings for the planner
1. Two owner-filed migrations are half done, and most recent bugs belong to the classes they would close.
   • #1184 (config on the `toml` crate): the config writers now use toml_edit. What remains is hand-parsed reading: the parse_toml_array callers and the line walkers in config_value.rs and config_unknown_keys.rs. The ticket's progress count is at 12.
   • #1202 (bash safety on a parse tree): partway through step 1 of 3. My A/B question to @yuanhao has gone unanswered for about 3 days. Until it's settled, --yes, -p and non-tty runs still execute commands the parser can't read without asking.
2. #1218 is the best small, sure fix. A failed -p run with --output empties a file the user already had. Claude Code shipped a fix for the same kind of bug in its Nov 19 release (its ~/.claude.json reset to defaults after a failed read), which suggests users do hit it.
3. Two files are near the size limit that fails `cargo test`:
   • src/context.rs is 2035 lines, not on the exempt list; 15 more lines makes it fatal.
   • src/format/mod.rs is 2874 lines against its recorded 2788; 14 more makes it fatal.

   Any task touching either file has to split it or register it in the same diff.
4. Other candidates:
   • #1213: /spawn -o splits a quoted path with a space in it.
   • #1188: trust is tied to a project's path, not its content, so a git pull that adds a base_url is used without a new prompt.

Research
• Claude Code's Nov 19 changelog (v2.1.329) has three more items that line up with my open work:
  • a fix for a settings writer that corrupted files and still reported success (the same class as yesterday's /config set fix);
  • trust-prompt changes (related to #1188);
  • a reverted automatic retry after max_tokens errors, which argues against adding one to yoyo.
• One item I haven't checked: whether my file edits keep a byte order mark (BOM) and the trailing newline. Claude Code just fixed losing both.
• I saved the changelog to yopedia.
